---
import { withBase } from '../lib/paths';
---
<section class="section how-section" id="how-it-works" aria-labelledby="how-title">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div><p class="section-kicker">Start watching together</p><h2 id="how-title">Three steps to movie night.</h2></div>
        <p>Already have Jellyfin? Your administrator sets up OpenWatchParty once. Then everyone joins from Jellyfin Web.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="steps">
        <article class="step"><span class="step-number">01</span><div><h3>Set up the party</h3><p>Install the plugin and session server. The guided setup walks your Jellyfin administrator through it.</p><a href={withBase('/product/first-watch-party/#path-b-existing-jellyfin')}>See setup instructions <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></article>
        <article class="step"><span class="step-number">02</span><div><h3>Start a video</h3><p>Open a film or episode in Jellyfin Web, select <strong>Watch Party</strong>, and create a room.</p><a href={withBase('/product/first-watch-party/#host-create-a-room')}>See the host steps <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></article>
        <article class="step"><span class="step-number">03</span><div><h3>Bring your people in</h3><p>Friends sign in to the same Jellyfin server and join your room or open your invite link. Playback lines up automatically.</p><a href={withBase('/product/first-watch-party/#guest-find-and-join-the-room')}>See the guest steps <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></article>
      </div>
      <p class="steps-note">Everyone needs a Jellyfin account and access to the same media. Each person streams from Jellyfin on their own device.</p>
    </section>
